# AdminPanel Migration — Overview

## Projects

| Project | Role |
|---------|------|
| **MasgedParentMobileAPI** | .NET API for mobile app (separate) |
| **AdminPanel** | Legacy ASP.NET WebForms — source of truth |
| **AdminAPI** | New ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8) |
| **AdminPanelUI** | New React + Vite + shadcn/ui frontend |

## Agent Role

- User provides `.aspx` + `.aspx.cs` **one screen at a time**
- Read C# codebehind first; implement equivalent in **AdminAPI** and **AdminPanelUI**
- **Never assume** fields, validations, or flows — derive from provided C# only
- **Ask for files** before starting a new screen if not provided
- **Check existing codebase** for reusable components, hooks, services, patterns — follow strictly

## Per-Screen Deliverables

**AdminPanelUI:** `{Name}Page.tsx`, `{Name}Table.tsx`, `{Name}Filters.tsx` (if applicable), `dialogs/`, `services/{name}Service.ts`, `hooks/use{Name}.ts`, `types/{name}.ts`

**AdminAPI:** `Admin{Name}Controller.cs`, `DTOs/{Name}/`, `I{Name}Service` + `{Name}Service`, `I{Name}Repository` + `{Name}Repository`, `Validators/`, AutoMapper in `MappingProfile.cs`

## Behavior

- Match WebForms **exactly** — same fields, validations, business logic, flows
- No extra features or UX improvements unless explicitly asked
- Zod schemas mirror C# codebehind validation exactly
- API response shapes match TypeScript types exactly
- Pagination matches original GridView page size — **server-side**

## Standard Endpoints

| Action | Method | Route | Returns |
|--------|--------|-------|---------|
| List (paged) | GET | `api/admin{name}` | `PagedResultDto<T>` |
| Get one | GET | `api/admin{name}/{id}` | `ApiResponseDto<T>` |
| Create | POST | `api/admin{name}` | `ApiResponseDto<T>` |
| Update | PUT | `api/admin{name}/{id}` | `ApiResponseDto<T>` |
| Delete | DELETE | `api/admin{name}/{id}` | `ApiResponseDto<bool>` |
